      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-58011",
      ":question/problem": "A fast-food seller decides to sell hamburgers cut into halves. Specific customers buy these hamburger halves during the final hour of the trading day. The table below shows the number of half-hamburgers each customer bought.\n\n| Customer | Half-Hamburgers |\n| --- | ---: |\n| Policeman | $3$ |\n| Teenager | $1$ |\n| Shop assistant | $3$ |\n\nGiven that each cross represents a different customer, what line plot shows the frequency of whole hamburgers sold?"
